cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
title: "sim_ce_core: a differentiable simulator of CT contrast-enhancement kinetics with Fisher-information identifiability analysis"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Institute-of-One/sim-ce-core"
url: "https://github.com/Institute-of-One/sim-ce-core"
authors:
  - family-names: Yamamoto
    given-names: Shuji
    email: yamamoto@lisit.jp
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9211-1071"
    affiliation: Institute of One, LISIT Co., Ltd., Tokyo, Japan
abstract: >
  A differentiable simulator of contrast-agent enhancement kinetics, built on a reduced
  descendant of Bae's compartmental CT-enhancement model, with the sensitivity, Fisher
  information and Cramer-Rao machinery to determine which physiological parameters a
  given CT sampling design can recover.
keywords:
  - contrast enhancement
  - pharmacokinetics
  - computed tomography
  - differentiable simulation
  - identifiability
  - Fisher information
  - experimental design
  - physics-informed neural networks
